WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.635
-Thank you so much
for joining us in studio, buddy.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.337
It's always good to see you.

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.672
Have you been able to move into
the new house yet?

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:08.975
-Yeah, man.
This is my first, like, time

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:12.178
living in an actual house,
and it's scary.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.646
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.381
-Wait. What do you mean?
Because you're used to what?

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:16.949
Apartments?
-Well, I'm used to noise,

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:20.119
I'm used to, like, ambulances
and fire trucks and all that.

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:21.554
[ Laughter ]
-That calms you down?

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.389
-Yeah! This is, like, scary

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:25.625
when you hear
just your house make noise.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.159
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.159 --> 00:00:29.562
There's like this ice maker
in the fridge thing or whatever,

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.097
and every time,
in the middle of the night,

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:32.165
when it's very still --
[ Audience member groans ]

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:33.165
-You know what
I'm talking about, right?

00:00:33.165 --> 00:00:34.634
[ Cheers ]

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.936
I always think I'm being robbed
by, like, The Three Stooges.

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:38.371
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.507
It sounds like someone falling
down the stairs every time.

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:41.674
It's scary.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:42.976
-You're being robbed
by The Three Stooges.

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.110
-Yeah, it's always loud
and clumsy.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.579
-[ Laughs ]
-But it's cool, it's cool.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.481
-Congratulations, bud.
I'm so happy for you.

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:51.083
Last time you were on the show,
you were here with Colin Jost,

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:53.786
and then, a few weeks later,
he got married.

00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:55.288
-Allegedly.

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:56.288
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.288 --> 00:00:57.957
-Now, don't say that.

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:00.059
-I still don't buy it, man.
-You were --

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:02.961
-He married Scarlett Johansson!
How's that possible? What?

00:01:02.961 --> 00:01:08.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.336
I don't think she knows
she's Scarlett Johansson.

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:12.738
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.738 --> 00:01:15.641
-Last time, you were saying that
you were gonna make a speech --

00:01:15.641 --> 00:01:18.043
-I wanted to. I wanted to, like,
interrupt the wedding.

00:01:18.043 --> 00:01:19.378
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:21.514
So if somebody said,
"Does anyone object with this?"

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:22.615
you were gonna stand up
and do your speech

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:23.883
and ruin his wedding.
-Yeah.

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.251
-Did you?
-No, I didn't.

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.819
Well, I had all these --
I wanted to.

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:28.421
I didn't have the courage.
-Yeah, good.

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:29.722
Smart.
-I had all of these pictures

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:31.257
of The Rock that I was gonna
send her, and be like,

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:35.127
"You could marry The Rock."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.127 --> 00:01:37.263
I still don't believe it.
I still think, at some point,

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:41.067
this is just, like, one long
Sacha Baron Cohen bit.

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:43.436
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.538
-You guys are great
on "Weekend Update" together.

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:49.074
I do love this one bit you do

00:01:49.074 --> 00:01:52.111
where you make Colin
read jokes that you wrote.

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:54.113
-Yeah.
-And he makes you read --

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:55.948
I mean, this is the best thing
I've ever seen.

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:58.317
-Yeah, we call it "Joke Swap."
-A joke swap.

00:01:58.317 --> 00:02:00.753
But I mean like, this --
How did that start?

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:03.022
-It was actually his idea,
which was kind of funny,

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:06.759
because I thought
he was trying to prank me.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.527
See, I'm paranoid.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.527 --> 00:02:10.163
-I think everything's a prank.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:11.764
Right now,
I think this is all a prank.

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:14.934
But he was like, "Hey,
why don't we do something

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.936
where, like,
you write jokes for me,

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:18.070
I write jokes for you,
and we don't know

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:19.272
till we get on air?"

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:21.106
And I'm like,
"Oh, you trying to set me up."

00:02:21.106 --> 00:02:22.541
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:02:22.541 --> 00:02:25.411
-So I started thinking of, like,
some really racist things

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:26.512
for him to say,
'cause I'm like...

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:27.914
[ Laughter ]
..."You not gonna get me.

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:29.849
You gonna catch some fire
coming in the door."

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.885
-Yeah, of course.
-And then we got on the air,

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:34.687
and a lot of his jokes
are kind of tame.

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:35.988
-And just nice,
and all yours are --

00:02:35.988 --> 00:02:38.391
-And all of mine was just,
like, about Rosa Parks.

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:41.361
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.863
I was like, "Oh, oh, okay.
That's one way to do it."

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:45.665
-Oh, my --
I mean, dude, his face,

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:46.899
you could just see him sweating.

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:49.435
-It was bright red,
and Black people loved it.

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:51.804
It's awesome.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.840
-It was just announced
that Elon Musk

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:57.643
is gonna host "SNL" May 8th.

00:02:57.643 --> 00:02:59.945
Are you --
With Miley Cyrus, by the way.

00:02:59.945 --> 00:03:01.214
-Yeah, no,
it's gonna be great.

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:03.049
-That's a big show.
Are you excited to meet him?

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:05.117
-I am excited to meet him.
I don't know if he knows,

00:03:05.117 --> 00:03:07.186
like -- usually, like,
we have this tradition --

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:08.721
I don't know, I think it's
in the book or whatever --

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:11.791
but at "Saturday Night Live,"
it's customary for hosts

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:14.293
to give, like, a couple million
dollars to the cast members.

00:03:14.293 --> 00:03:15.961
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:17.663
Wow.
-Yeah, I don't know if he's --

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:20.299
if he's a cool guy,
maybe he'll...

00:03:20.299 --> 00:03:21.934
-Keep up that tradition.
-Yeah, maybe.

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:24.570
-Yeah, that's so smart.
See, that's smart, yeah.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:27.039
-He's going to Mars, man.
He doesn't need all that money.

00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:29.976
-Would you ever go to space?
-No, not on purpose.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.644
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.679
-Wait. How would you get there
on accident?

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:34.947
-I don't know.
-Go to L.A., next thing

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:36.716
you're like,
"Wait. Is that Earth?"

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:39.218
[ Laughter ]
-No, yeah, I don't know.

00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:41.086
I wouldn't.
Would you?

00:03:41.086 --> 00:03:42.788
-I thought about it.
No.

00:03:42.788 --> 00:03:45.224
-If the richest man in the world
is going, would you go?

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:46.692
-No.
-Okay.

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:49.695
-I'd go maybe, like,
the year after

00:03:49.695 --> 00:03:50.897
the richest man in the world.
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:53.131
-I'll go when they build
a CVS there.

00:03:53.131 --> 00:03:56.402
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:58.838
-Until that, no.
-Yeah, until they have a CVS,

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:00.072
I don't trust it.

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:01.874
-I want to talk about this show
on HBO Max.

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:03.943
I'm so psyched
that you made this.

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.978
It's called
"That Damn Michael Che."

00:04:05.978 --> 00:04:07.614
-Yeah.
-Which is so funny

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:09.782
even just saying that title,
because the audience was like,

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.651
"Why would you say that
about Michael Che?"

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:13.852
-That's why I like it!
Because it could go either way.

00:04:13.852 --> 00:04:15.655
It could be like, "Man,
that damn Michael Che is funny,"

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:17.290
or it could be,
"That damn Michael Che."

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:18.725
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:20.826
I like the kind of weight of it.

00:04:20.826 --> 00:04:22.494
-It's great.
What is it like?

00:04:22.494 --> 00:04:23.796
What do you compare it to?

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.898
-I wanted to call it
"That Black-Ass Michael Che."

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.066
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, okay, yeah.

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:29.168
-But HBO said no.
-No, yeah.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:30.602
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.602 --> 00:04:31.971
-Is it sketch?
Is it stand-up?

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:35.307
What is it?
-It's like loose kind of jokes.

00:04:35.307 --> 00:04:36.476
-Yeah.
-And then there's also

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:38.811
some sketches.
And it's just fun, you know?

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:40.847
It's like six episodes.

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:42.047
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.047 --> 00:04:43.116
-I want everyone to watch.

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:44.650
-Yeah, I want everybody
to watch it.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:46.151
Please, watch it!
It's fun.

00:04:46.151 --> 00:04:48.454
-Make sure you get on this.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:50.956
HBO, HBO Max.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:50.956 --> 00:04:52.391
Here's Michael Che...
-You got a clip?

00:04:52.391 --> 00:04:53.959
-...in his new show --
Yeah, you got a clip.

00:04:53.959 --> 00:04:55.328
You never come on with a clip.

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:58.197
-No, it's so weird to be out
here to promote something.

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:00.299
-Yeah, you never are.
-No, I'm not.

00:05:00.299 --> 00:05:01.333
I'm just hanging out with you.
-Wait. This is history.

00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:02.668
We're actually
throwing to a clip.

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:05.638
-Yeah, this is crazy.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:06.972
-This is a big deal.

00:05:06.972 --> 00:05:08.674
-I'm on the "The Tonight Show,"
going to a clip.

00:05:08.674 --> 00:05:11.644
-Yeah.
Here's Michael Che

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:13.313
in his new show,
"That Damn Michael Che."

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:15.348
Take a look.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:26.792
-I just want to say I'm sorry.

00:05:26.792 --> 00:05:28.961
-Oh, it's -- it's cool.
I could barely smell it.

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:31.097
-What?
Oh, no, not that.

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:35.100
Um, I mean,
I'm sorry for everything

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:36.468
going on in the country.

00:05:36.468 --> 00:05:38.570
[ Dramatic music plays ]

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:43.342
With the police shootings
and all the injustices.

00:05:43.342 --> 00:05:48.213
And for white privilege.

00:05:48.213 --> 00:05:49.715
-This thing even move yet?

00:05:49.715 --> 00:05:54.086
-I'm an ally, obviously,
so I'm not trying to be weird.

00:05:54.086 --> 00:05:56.822
-Think it's supposed
to light up if it's moving.

00:05:56.822 --> 00:05:58.858
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:02.428
-Stuck on an elevator.
[ Laughs ]

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:04.630
Michael Che, everybody!
All episodes of

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:09.869
"That Damn Michael Che" are
streaming May 6th on HBO Max.

